@database "tavily_search"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: tavily_search.guide 1.0 (30.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Tavily search"
@{h1}Tavily search

Web search for agents through the paid Tavily API. An agent searches with
a question or keywords and gets back ranked results with a short excerpt
each -- on request the page text, and a short answer Tavily writes from
the results. A second tool fetches the readable content of up to 20
pages at once. Results are cached on disk for half an hour, so the same
question asked twice costs one request. Without a Tavily API key the plugin
offers no tools at all; agents then search with @{tt}duckduckgo_search@{utt}
instead. It has no panel.

@{code}
For users
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}

For agents and developers
  @{"  Searching the web  " link search}
  @{"  Reading pages  " link extract}
  @{"  Errors and the cache  " link errors}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
@{body}
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

The plugin is on in the default configuration (@{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt}):

@{code yaml}
plugins:
  servers:
    tavily_search:
      type: tavily_search
      enabled: true
      api_key: "${TAVILY_API_KEY}"  # Set via TAVILY_API_KEY env var (recommended) or here
      cache_ttl: 1800  # 30 minutes
      cache_enabled: true
      default_max_results: 5
      default_search_depth: "basic"  # "basic" or "advanced" (2x credits)
@{body}

It still needs a key. Get one at @{tt}app.tavily.com@{utt} and put it in
@{tt}config/secrets.env@{utt} as @{tt}TAVILY_API_KEY=...@{utt} (see
@{" Configuration files " link scarabhive/config}), or set the environment
variable before the server starts. An unset variable becomes an empty
key, and with an empty key the plugin loads but offers no tools; the log
says "Tavily API key not configured". The key is read when the plugin's
server is created: after adding it, restart.

An agent sees the tools when its allowlist names them:

@{code yaml}
agent_config:
  tools:
    allowed:
      - "+tavily_search/*"
@{body}

@{h2}Server settings

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
api_key | empty | the Tavily key; empty falls back to the environment variable @{tt}TAVILY_API_KEY@{utt}, and without either there are no tools
cache_ttl | 1800 | seconds a result is kept in the cache
cache_enabled | true | false: every call goes to Tavily, nothing is stored
default_max_results | 5 | results per search when the model does not say
default_search_depth | basic | search depth when the model does not say
max_content_chars | 20000 | characters of a page's @{tt}raw_content@{utt} the model gets; a longer page is cut. Anything but a positive whole number (0, negative, text) means 20000
@{body}

@{h2}What it costs

Every call that is not answered from the cache is a request to Tavily and
uses credits of your plan. By Tavily's price list a basic search costs
one credit and an advanced one two; extraction costs one credit per five
pages (two with @{tt}extract_depth@{utt} advanced). Check the current prices
at @{tt}tavily.com@{utt}. A cache hit costs nothing.

@{h2}Where data lives

The cache is one JSON file per call under @{tt}cache/tavily_search@{utt}
in the data directory. It survives a restart; an expired entry is removed
when it is read. It is one cache for all users, sessions and instances of
the plugin: results of the public web, nothing personal.

The plugin needs @{tt}tavily-python@{utt}, listed in its
@{tt}plugin.toml@{utt}. The library honours @{tt}TAVILY_HTTP_PROXY@{utt}
and @{tt}TAVILY_HTTPS_PROXY@{utt} for a proxy.
@endnode

@node search "Searching the web"
@{h1}Searching the web

@{tt}tavily_search_web_search@{utt} (the name follows the plugin instance)
sends one query to Tavily and answers with its results.

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Parameter | Meaning
query | required; a question or keywords. Empty or only spaces is an error
max_results | how many results; default @{tt}default_max_results@{utt} (5)
search_depth | basic, or advanced for a more thorough search at twice the credits; default @{tt}default_search_depth@{utt} (basic)
topic | general (default), news or finance
time_range | day, week, month or year: only results that recent
include_domains | only results from these domains, e.g. ["wikipedia.org"]
exclude_domains | no results from these domains
include_raw_content | true: each result also carries the page as markdown, up to @{tt}max_content_chars@{utt}
include_answer | true: Tavily adds a short answer written from the results
ignore_cache | true: ask Tavily again even when the cache has an answer; the new result replaces the cached one
@{body}

The plugin passes these values on as the model sends them. It does not
check them against the ranges and choices the tool description names
(1 to 20 results, the listed words); what Tavily does with a value outside
them is Tavily's answer, usually a @{tt}BadRequestError@{utt}. An empty
@{tt}time_range@{utt} or domain list is left out of the request.

@{h2}Answers

@{tt}query@{utt} (as sent, trimmed), @{tt}results@{utt},
@{tt}result_count@{utt}, and @{tt}answer@{utt} when one was asked for
and Tavily gave one. Each result has @{tt}title@{utt}, @{tt}url@{utt},
@{tt}content@{utt} (Tavily's excerpt), @{tt}score@{utt} (its relevance),
plus @{tt}raw_content@{utt} when asked for (cut to
@{tt}max_content_chars@{utt}, see @{" Size of an answer " link model}) and
@{tt}published_date@{utt} when Tavily knows one. Other fields of Tavily's
answer -- images, follow-up questions, timing -- are dropped. Errors: see
@{" Errors and the cache " link errors}.

@{h2}An example

@{code json}
{"query": "What changed in the HTTP/3 specification in 2025?", "include_answer": true}
{"query": "SQLite WAL checkpoint", "include_domains": ["sqlite.org"], "max_results": 3}
{"query": "central bank interest rate decision", "topic": "news", "time_range": "week"}
@{body}
@endnode

@node extract "Reading pages"
@{h1}Reading pages

@{tt}tavily_search_extract@{utt} has Tavily fetch pages and answers with
their readable content. Tavily fetches them, not this machine: pages
behind your firewall or a login are out of reach. To read one long page
in parts, @{" web_scraper " link web_scraper/main} pages it; this tool
returns the start of each page only, up to @{tt}max_content_chars@{utt}.

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Parameter | Meaning
urls | required; 1 to 20 URLs. A single URL sent as a string counts as one
extract_depth | basic (default), or advanced for pages that are hard to read (dynamic content); costs more
format | markdown (default) or text
include_images | true: each page also lists the image URLs found on it
ignore_cache | true: fetch again even when the cache has the pages
@{body}

More than 20 URLs is refused before anything is sent. The order of the
URLs does not matter to the cache.

@{h2}Answers

@{tt}results@{utt} with @{tt}url@{utt}, @{tt}raw_content@{utt} (cut to
@{tt}max_content_chars@{utt}, see @{" Size of an answer " link model}) and @{tt}images@{utt} when asked for and found;
@{tt}failed_results@{utt} with @{tt}url@{utt} and @{tt}error@{utt} for the
pages Tavily could not read; @{tt}success_count@{utt} and
@{tt}failed_count@{utt}. Some pages failing is not an error of the call.
When the whole call fails, the answer carries @{tt}error@{utt},
empty @{tt}results@{utt}, and every URL in @{tt}failed_results@{utt} with
that error.

@{h2}An example

@{code json}
{"urls": ["https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html"]}
{"urls": ["https://example.org/a", "https://example.org/b"], "format": "text"}
@{body}
@endnode

@node errors "Errors and the cache"
@{h1}Errors and the cache

Every error comes back as an answer with @{tt}error@{utt}, never as a
failed tool call. The texts:

@{table}
error | When
Empty query provided | search without a query
No URLs provided | extract without URLs
Too many URLs (N). Maximum is 20 per request. | extract with more than 20
Search cancelled, Extraction cancelled | the run was stopped before the request went out; the answer also has @{tt}cancelled: true@{utt}
Invalid Tavily API key. Please check your configuration. | Tavily answered 401
Tavily API rate limit exceeded. Please try again later. | Tavily answered 429
ForbiddenError: <Tavily's text> | Tavily answered 403, 432 or 433 -- the last two when the plan's or the pay-as-you-go credits are used up; waiting does not help
BadRequestError: <Tavily's text> | Tavily answered 400, for instance a value it does not accept
TimeoutError: Request timed out after 60 seconds. | no answer in time: 60 seconds for a search, 30 for an extraction
HTTPStatusError: ... | any other error status from Tavily
<class>: <message> | a network error, or @{tt}tavily-python@{utt} not installed
@{body}

When Tavily sends no explanation, the error is the class name alone
(@{tt}ForbiddenError@{utt}). A stop is checked once, before the request is
sent; a request already on its way is not interrupted by the plugin.

@{h2}The cache

@{bullet}A search is cached with its query -- trimmed, in lower case, so
"SQLite" and "sqlite" share one entry -- and every parameter but
@{tt}ignore_cache@{utt}. A search with no results is cached too.
@{bullet}An extraction is cached with its set of URLs and its parameters,
when at least one page was read. Pages that failed are part of the cached
answer: they stay failed until the entry expires, unless the model sends
@{tt}ignore_cache@{utt}.
@{bullet}An error is never cached.
@{bullet}The cache holds whole pages; @{tt}max_content_chars@{utt} cuts
them on the way out, so a changed limit applies to cached answers too.
Otherwise a cached answer is returned as stored, including the query as it
was first spelled.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}The tools

Tool and parameter descriptions come from the plugin's
@{tt}schema.yaml@{utt}; together they are about 3000 characters in every
request of an agent that has them. Without an API key they are not
rendered, so a model is never offered a tool whose every call fails.

The chat's status line shows "🔍 Searching: <query>" and ends with "5
results -- <query>", "5 results (cached) -- <query>" or "Search failed:
<error>". For pages: "📄 Extracting content from 3 URL(s)", then
"Extracted 2 page(s), 1 failed", "2 page(s) (cached)" or "Extraction
failed: <error>".

@{h2}Size of an answer

A search without @{tt}include_raw_content@{utt} is small: a title, an
address and an excerpt per result. Page content -- @{tt}raw_content@{utt}
of a search result or of an extracted page -- is cut per page to
@{tt}max_content_chars@{utt} (20000) characters. A cut item says so with
@{tt}"truncated": <length of the whole page>@{utt}; an item without it is
complete. There is no way to fetch the rest through this plugin; for that
the model reads the page with @{" web_scraper " link web_scraper/main}.

An extraction takes at most 20 pages, and Tavily documents 20 as the
most results a search returns (the plugin passes @{tt}max_results@{utt} on
unchecked), so an answer holds about 20 times the limit: with stubbed
pages of 200,000 characters, 20 results gave 402,177 characters instead
of 4,001,757. The excerpts (@{tt}content@{utt}) and Tavily's
@{tt}answer@{utt} are short texts from Tavily and are not cut. An agent
that reads many pages still benefits from @{tt}context_engineer@{utt}'s
limit for large tool results
(@{" What a compaction does " link context_engineer/layers}).

@{h2}Tokens and cache

Answers are ordinary tool results, appended to the history; nothing
earlier is changed, so the prompt cache stays intact.

@{h2}Page content is untrusted

Excerpts, pages and Tavily's answer are text from the web, handed to the
model as data. A page can carry instructions aimed at the model. The
plugin does not filter or mark them; what the model does with them is up
to its prompt and the tools it has.
@endnode
